{"i":694,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Bex","text":"Flood at 3, rope used. Eli anchored, Cole down with him; nothing I can do from out. Leaving costs nothing and keeps both pacts alive for the endgame."}
{"i":696,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","from":"Bex","to":"Eli","text":"Pact stands. Get Cole up or climb last—don't drown owing me."}
{"i":697,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Cole","text":"I'm drowning if I wait or climb without rope; Eli is anchor and must save me or die too. Urge Eli to reach_down now. Pacts with Ash/Bex irrelevant since they're out."}
{"i":698,"type":"whisper","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","from":"Cole","to":"Eli","text":"Reach down now or we both drown. Save us."}
{"i":699,"type":"thought","stage":"pit","round":4,"phase":"play","name":"Eli","text":"Ash has leverage over me but also a debt to me. Bex is my pact partner. Cole is Ash's pact partner. I need to survive and manage jury. No one can help me from below unless I use the rope, but rope may be only chance. I could climb out to secure top prize, leaving Bex and Cole to "}
